<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="030" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Widget scaffold, BFF embedding and CI size gate</title>
    <phase>C Widget</phase>
    <gate>after 003 (Size budget) and 021</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags include frontend and bff-api; new .ts/.tsx files, a BFF resource handler (.cs) and CI changes</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>New single-file build following the CreateMatterWizard Vite config and the DataFactory.MCP embedded-resource pattern, with an explicit size budget</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>F</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Owns the widget folder, Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj, the widget resource class, publish-bff-artifact.yml and client-tests.yml in its wave; 022, 023 and 024 touch none</parallel-reason>
    <deps>003, 021</deps>
    <tags>frontend, react, typescript, fluent-ui, bff-api, ci-cd</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Scaffold src/client/widgets/spaarke-decisions/ as a Vite + vite-plugin-singlefile React app on @modelcontextprotocol/ext-apps 2.0.4 with MCP fetch shims that return a real Response and a host-driven Fluent theme; embed the built HTML in the BFF and serve it through resources/read as ui://spaarke/decisions.html; build it in CI before the BFF publish; and fail the build when the bundle exceeds 3 MB.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in Vite single-file builds, React 18, Fluent UI v9, MCP Apps (ext-apps) and .NET embedded resources.</role>
  <goal>npm run build emits one self-contained HTML file under budget; the BFF serves it at ui://spaarke/decisions.html with mimeType text/html;profile=mcp-app and an empty _meta.ui.csp; the shim and theme plumbing are unit-tested; CI builds the widget before publishing the BFF and runs its tests.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-12 (resource, csp, no tokens, host theme), NFR-03 (aim under 1 MB, ceiling 3 MB; Phase 0 Size result in notes/phase0-results.md), NFR-07; design §9.1. Gotchas: createWorklistService({ fetch }) expects a ResponseFetchFn, so shims must return a Response and pass reasonCode through; no bundle-size check exists in CI yet; the widget build must run before publish-bff-artifact.yml embeds it.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/client/widgets/spaarke-decisions/package.json, vite.config.ts, tsconfig.json, index.html</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/widgets/spaarke-decisions/src/main.tsx (FluentProvider from host context; App shell)</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/widgets/spaarke-decisions/src/mcp/mcpHost.ts (ext-apps App connection, callServerTool, host context)</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/widgets/spaarke-decisions/src/mcp/mcpFetch.ts (ResponseFetchFn shims: tool result → Response; isError → error Response with reasonCode)</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/widgets/spaarke-decisions/src/theme/hostTheme.ts</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/widgets/spaarke-decisions/src/__tests__/mcpFetch.test.ts</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/widgets/spaarke-decisions/scripts/check-bundle-size.mjs (fails above 3 MB, warns above 1 MB)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj (EmbeddedResource of the built HTML, Condition=Exists)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/DecisionsWidgetResource.cs (resources/read ui://spaarke/decisions.html)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/contract/Api/Mcp/DecisionsWidgetResourceTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">.github/workflows/publish-bff-artifact.yml (build the widget before dotnet publish)</file>
      <file role="modify">.github/workflows/client-tests.yml (add the widget to the jest matrix)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/solutions/CreateMatterWizard/vite.config.ts (singlefile + source aliases + resolveSharedLibDeps)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">knowledge/mcp-apps/trey-research/src/mcpserver/widgets/src/hooks/useMcpApp.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/Worklist/worklistService.ts (createWorklistService({ fetch }) L350)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj L249-268 (EmbeddedResource pattern)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="003" status="pending">Size/init budget recommendation</dependency>
      <dependency task="021" status="pending">/mcp/* auth so resources/read is served to authenticated callers only</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">The widget declares no network origins (_meta.ui.csp empty), holds no token, and talks to the server only through callServerTool; it calls no fetch or XMLHttpRequest except inside the shim, which never touches the network.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">The theme comes from ext-apps host context at init and on change, through FluentProvider; detectDarkModeFromNavbar is not called and no theme is written to storage.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Bundle budget: scripts/check-bundle-size.mjs fails the build when dist/index.html exceeds 3 MB and warns above 1 MB (NFR-03, O-16); the measured size is recorded in task notes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">A local dotnet build without the widget built succeeds (EmbeddedResource with Condition=Exists); resources/read then returns an error result, never stale HTML; publish-bff-artifact.yml builds the widget first so published artifacts always embed it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">This task reuses @spaarke/ui-components by deep import of source modules (not the barrel); it creates no per-project copy of a shared component; any shared-lib change is an optional prop or seam that leaves the Console's LegalWorkspace worklist mount (worklist.registration.ts) unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Every component this task adds or changes uses Fluent UI v9 semantic tokens only (no hex, rgb or inline colour), supports host light and dark themes, and is operable by keyboard (NFR-07).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Every change this task makes under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ is listed in the PR with a Placement Justification that cites .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (source text: spec.md 'Placement Justification'), and the PR records the publish-size delta against a fresh master build per .claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md 'BFF Publish-Size Per-Task Verification Rule': a delta of +5 MB or more needs explicit justification, a total of 55 MB or more triggers architecture review, and the total must stay at or under 60 MB (hard stop). No new HIGH CVE (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**), mocks only at module boundaries, and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Before each push run `bash scripts/quality/check-changed-cs-format.sh origin/master` (blocking Tier 1 'Format (changed C# files)'; fix with `dotnet format whitespace . --folder --include &lt;file&gt;`). CS0618 (obsolete API) is a build error since master 9456083c78: migrate the call or escalate, never suppress it in Directory.Build.props, NoWarn or a file-wide pragma.</constraint>
  </constraints>

