  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read the Phase 0 Size result and the spike note's ext-apps 2.0.4 API notes.</step>
    <step order="2">Scaffold the widget folder mirroring CreateMatterWizard's vite.config.ts (singlefile, aliases to @spaarke/ui-components source, React version boundary); npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund.</step>
    <step order="3">Implement mcpHost.ts (connect, host context, callServerTool) and mcpFetch.ts (ResponseFetchFn: map a request path + method to a tool call; wrap structuredContent in a Response; map isError to a non-2xx Response whose JSON body carries reasonCode and message).</step>
    <step order="4">Implement hostTheme.ts and main.tsx (FluentProvider with webLightTheme/webDarkTheme from host context; placeholder App until 031).</step>
    <step order="5">Add check-bundle-size.mjs to the build; add unit tests for the shim and the theme.</step>
    <step order="6">Embed dist/index.html in the BFF (Condition=Exists) and add DecisionsWidgetResource for resources/read; add the contract test.</step>
    <step order="7">Wire CI: widget build before dotnet publish in publish-bff-artifact.yml; widget in the client-tests.yml jest matrix.</step>
    <step order="8">Run the ui-tests below against a local MCP Apps host; measure the publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="9">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="10">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If ext-apps 2.0.4's API differs from the 1.x samples so that callServerTool or host context is not available as assumed, STOP and record the drift with a proposed adapter before building on it (risk R13).</trigger>
    <trigger>If the empty scaffold plus Fluent already exceeds 1 MB, STOP and report the composition before 031 adds the lane.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Code-page Vite builds (src/solutions/CreateMatterWizard/vite.config.ts, ten code pages); no MCP App widget exists in src/ (ls src/client/widgets returns nothing).</existing>
    <extension>Same toolchain and shared components, new entry point: a code page runs inside Dataverse with Xrm, while the widget runs in a sandboxed Copilot frame that only speaks MCP, so it cannot be a code page.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>There is no UI to view or resolve a Work Item in Copilot or Cowork (FR-12, FR-13), and NFR-03 has no enforcement.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Widget shell renders in a local MCP Apps host">
      <url>http://localhost:{basic-host-port}/?server={local-bff}/mcp/legal-operations</url>
      <steps>
        <step>Start the BFF locally with Mcp:Enabled=true and a dev test token</step>
        <step>Open the ext-apps basic host pointed at /mcp/legal-operations and load ui://spaarke/decisions.html</step>
        <step>Verify the shell renders and a shimmed call round-trips through callServerTool</step>
        <step>Check the browser console for JavaScript errors</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The shell renders with no console errors; no network request leaves the frame (devtools Network tab shows none)</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Switch the host (Cowork or the local MCP Apps host) to dark theme</step>
        <step>Verify backgrounds adapt (no white surface in dark mode) and text adapts (no black text in dark mode)</step>
        <step>Verify icons use currentColor</step>
        <step>Switch back to light theme and verify the widget follows without reload</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>All colours come from Fluent v9 semantic tokens driven by host context (ADR-021); nothing is stored</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Install (npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund), build and test TypeScript projects</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET projects (dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/, dotnet test)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/widgets/spaarke-decisions/</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/DecisionsWidgetResource.cs</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/widgets/spaarke-decisions/src/__tests__/mcpFetch.test.ts</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Api/Mcp/DecisionsWidgetResourceTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">npm run build in the widget folder emits a single dist/index.html with all JS and CSS inline; its size is recorded and is under 3 MB.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a build whose output exceeds 3 MB fails check-bundle-size.mjs (test with a padded fixture).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">resources/read for ui://spaarke/decisions.html returns mimeType text/html;profile=mcp-app, an empty _meta.ui.csp and the built HTML.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: with the widget not built, dotnet build succeeds and resources/read returns an error result (not stale HTML).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">mcpFetch returns a Response with status 200 and the tool's structuredContent for success, and a non-2xx Response whose JSON carries reasonCode and message for an isError result (unit tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no code outside mcpFetch.ts calls fetch or XMLHttpRequest, and no token is read or stored (grep + test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The theme follows host context light and dark and nothing is written to localStorage or sessionStorage for theme.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">publish-bff-artifact.yml builds the widget before dotnet publish; client-tests.yml runs the widget's tests.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ext-apps 2.0.4 API drift notes are recorded in the task notes; the PR records the BFF publish-size delta (at or under 60 MB).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Node installs in src/solutions/* and similar use npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund (root CLAUDE.md §12). Deep-import @spaarke/ui-components source so pdfjs-dist, mammoth and App Insights stay out of the bundle (design §9.1).</notes>

